{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 910 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7aa924ec3bc12ea0c8fd48da930157c10af1cefc3c7980fbc5f5c88601877299" :edb/db-before-t 909 :edb/db-after-t 910 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534222 50 #inst "2026-10-06T14:52:59.053Z" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114865 1100 "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ if $y = 2 \\,\\textrm {arccot } x.$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114865 1100 "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ if $y = 2 \\,\\textrm {arccot} x$." 13194139534222 false] [17592186114865 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114865 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot} x) = -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2arccotx) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(arccotx) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1 + x^{2}}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{1 + x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 false] [17592186114869 1100 "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec } x}{\\textrm{arccsc } x},$ calculate $f'(x).$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114869 1100 "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec} x}{\\textrm{arccsc} x}$, calculate $f'(x)$." 13194139534222 false] [17592186114869 1145 "Here, we let\n\n$$\nu(x) = \\textrm{arcsec} x\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nv(x) = \\textrm{arccsc} x\n$$\n\n, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) = \\dfrac 1 {\\begin{vmatrix}x & \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad v'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {\\mid x\\end{vmatrix} \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (u^{′}(x) \\cdot v(x) - u(x) \\cdot v^{′}(x))/([v(x)]^{2}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{1}{\\begin{vmatrix}x & \\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}} \\cdot arccscx - arcsecx \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\mid x\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}))/(arccsc^{2}x) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{1}{\\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}})\\frac{arccscx + arcsecx}{arccsc^{2}x} \\\\ = \\frac{arccscx + arcsecx}{\\mid x\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}arccsc^{2}x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 false] [17592186114869 1145 "Here, we let $u(x) = \\textrm{arcsec } x$ and $v(x) = \\textrm{arccsc } x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) =  \\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\t\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\tv'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\text{arccsc }x-\\text{arcsec }x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}{\\text{ arccsc }}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114872 1100 "If $f(x) =3 x\\, \\textrm {arccsc }x,$ calculate $f'(x).$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114872 1100 "If $f(x) =3 x\\, \\textrm {arccsc}x$, calculate $f'(x)$." 13194139534222 false] [17592186114872 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccsc } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}} \\, .\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3(x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc }x)+\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)) \\\\  & =3x(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114872 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccsc} x) = -\\dfrac 1 {\\mid x \\mid \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}} \\,\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3xarccscx) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(xarccscx) \\\\\n&= 3(x \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(arccscx) + arccscx \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x)) \\\\\n&= 3x(-\\frac{1}{\\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}}) + 3arccscx \\cdot 1 \\\\ =-\\frac{3x}{\\mid x\\end{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x^{2} - 1}} + 3arccscx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 false] [17592186114874 1100 "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) =2 \\, \\textrm {arccot } (x^2 + 5).$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114874 1100 "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) =2 \\, \\textrm {arccot} (x^2 + 5)$." 13194139534222 false] [17592186114874 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }({x}^{2}+5)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+26}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186114874 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot} x) = -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2arccot(x^{2} + 5)) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot (- (1)/(1 + (x^{2} + 5)^{2})) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} + 5) \\\\\n&= - (2)/(1 + (x^{2} + 5)^{2}) \\cdot 2x \\\\\n&= - (4x)/(1 + (x^{2} + 5)^{2}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{4x}{x^{4} + 10x^{2} + 26}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 false] [17592186115314 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282707 13194139534222 true] [17592186115314 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282714 13194139534222 true] [17592186115314 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282763 13194139534222 true] [17592186115314 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282782 13194139534222 true] [17592186115314 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282795 13194139534222 true] [17592186115315 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282721 13194139534222 true] [17592186115315 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282742 13194139534222 true] [17592186115315 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282770 13194139534222 true] [17592186115315 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282802 13194139534222 true] [17592186115315 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282809 13194139534222 true] [17592186115316 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282728 13194139534222 true] [17592186115316 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282735 13194139534222 true] [17592186115316 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282749 13194139534222 true] [17592186115316 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282756 13194139534222 true] [17592186115316 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282792 13194139534222 true] [17592186115317 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282767 13194139534222 true] [17592186115317 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282775 13194139534222 true] [17592186115317 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282785 13194139534222 true] [17592186115317 1020 #edb/ref 17592186282789 13194139534222 true] [17592186115658 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534222 true] [17592186115658 1100 "Calculate $f^{′}(x)$ for $f(x) = 2\\arccsc(8 - x^{4})$." 13194139534222 false] [17592186115658 1100 "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=2arccsc(8-{x}^{4}).$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186115658 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc}\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot (-4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282708 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1089 "q-110510" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1100 "Find the slope of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=-7arccscx$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1113 #uuid "da33d32a-51d8-587d-b45c-abd810d5a74c" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282707 1145 "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7arccscx) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{7}{|\\sqrt{5}|\\sqrt{{\\sqrt{5}}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282709 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282710 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282711 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282712 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282713 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1041 "selection" 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282709 13194139534222 true] [17592186282708 1110 #uuid "3f